extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts World Book 4: Africa printed 117-118 (cache p118-p119), read off
    the text layer and checked against 130 dpi renders of both pages. The
    brief named 117-119; the entry ends on printed 118, where the Tree People
    R.C.C. begins, so source_book says 117-118.
  - xp_table: the "Agogwe & Crocodillians" ladder on printed 160, read off a
    300 dpi render of that column; lower bounds 0, 1,826 ... 280,501 (L15
    tops out at 320,500).
  - PSIONIC TIERS ARE THREE CHOOSABLE ABILITIES, NOT VARIANTS. The brief asked
    for `variants`, but VARIANT_OVERRIDES (js/parser.js) does not include
    `psionics`, and the model it named, add-shaydor-spherian-class.sql, itself
    uses one choose-1 special ability per orientation, each carrying a full
    psionics block, for exactly that reason. This class copies that shape and
    carries no class-level psionics block.
  - THE PERCENTILE ROLL is not stored or enforced: the app has no roll for it.
    Each ability''s name carries its percentage and its description the roll
    range (01-60 minor, 61-97 major, 98-00 master); the player rolls d100 at
    creation and takes the matching ability. A GM who prefers can assign it.
  - Major: "select a total of six powers from the healing and/or sensitive
    categories, plus" Sense Evil, Sixth Sense and Mind Block, so the six are
    picked and the three are granted (powers_starting 6). Master: 4 Super +
    4 Sensitive + 4 Physical as powers_starting_groups (12), plus one from
    those three categories at levels 2, 4, 6 ... 14.
  - I.S.P.: minor M.E. + 12 +1D6/level; major M.E. + 20 +2D6/level; master
    M.E. + 40 +3D6/level, as printed.
  - The entry heads its list "O.C.C. Abilities & Bonuses"; it is an R.C.C.
    with its own skill list ("Wilderness Man R.C.C. Skills"), related and
    secondary skills, equipment and money line, so it is played without an
    O.C.C. and both skill blocks are stored as printed.
  - men_of_arms false: a race. "+20 S.D.C." is a pool bonus (pools.sdc 20);
    no hit point or S.D.C. formula is printed. P.P.E. 2D6.
  - Bonuses: +2 initiative; "+2 to save vs all types of poisons and disease"
    as toxins_poisons 2 and disease 2.
  - Skills: bases are catalog base plus the printed bonus. Gobblely at 75%
    and native tongue at 98% are fixed figures (per_level 0). Track Animals
    is Track & Trap Animals; Fish is Fishing; Swim and Climb are Swimming
    and Climbing. Land Navigation is stored at the jungle figure (+15%, 51);
    the +5% elsewhere is in its note. No literacy is printed; none stored.
    W.P. Ancient of choice is a choose-1 from the ancient W.P. rows (W.P.
    Blunt and Targeting are already granted, so they are left out).
  - Hand to Hand: Basic, changeable to Expert for one other skill; no other
    style is offered, so hand_to_hand costs { expert: 1 }.
  - Related: three, plus two at level 2 and one each at 4, 8 and 12.
    Secondary: none at level 1, three at level 3 and three at level 9 (three
    at EACH level). Pilot "horsemanship, water vessels and hover vehicles
    only" is Horsemanship: General (its own catalog category) plus the
    civilian boat rows, Water Scooters, Hover Craft (ground) and Hovercycles,
    Skycycles & Rocket Bikes; submersibles, warships and water skiing are
    left out as a judgement call. Rogue except computer and streetwise
    excludes Computer Hacking, Streetwise and Streetwise: Drugs; Rogue +2% is
    as printed (the Tree People print +5%). Physical excludes S.C.U.B.A. as
    the catalog row SCUBA. Technical "lore and language only" is Language:
    Other plus every Lore row the catalog files under Technical (Lore: American
    Indians and Lore: Cattle & Animals are filed under Cowboy and left out).
  - Equipment: loincloth as clothing, the 30 ft rope as lightweight-rope,
    the sack as sack, and the spear as wooden-spear. The rope belt is not
    stored (the only belt row is palladium-fantasy). The war club or 1D4
    throwing sticks is prose in side_effects: the catalog has no Rifts war
    club or throwing-stick row (war-club is palladium-fantasy), and no stub
    was created. The 10% chances of modern gear and weapons are prose.
  - No starting money: "Money: None."
