# Agogwe

## Lore

The agogwe are small, hair-covered australopithecine humanoids, the
prehistoric forebears of humankind, long believed extinct. They survived in
the dense forests of the Congo and, to a lesser degree, the forests and plains
of Uganda, Tanzania and Zambia. With modern man gone and the forests left to
spread for three centuries, their numbers have risen to perhaps a quarter of a
million, scattered in tiny nomadic clans of 4D4x10.

They are quick and agile, mostly gatherers of fruit, nuts, roots and leaves
who also hunt small game, birds and fish. Their tribes have elders, a chief,
and a medicine man or priests, but no rain makers and no king or queen. They
are gentle, family-minded and peaceful, though fierce in defence of the tribe.
Their only true friends are the tree people; they regard the pygmies as
harmless neighbours but are too timid to seek them out, and they shun the
outside world.

Every agogwe is psychic, which is likely how they stayed hidden for so long.

## GM Notes

Roll percentile for the psionic tier at creation: 01-60 minor, 61-97 major,
98-00 master. Master psionics are frequently tribal leaders. Agogwe fear magic
and the supernatural, can be bullied by those who wield them, and never use
magic items.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'agogwe');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'agogwe';

